---
// Same weights, two readouts: token-by-token prose for a person vs one typed distribution for software.
// Probabilities are the example response in TypeSafe's docs. Used in "The Answer Was Already in the Weights".
const prose = ['Sure', '!', ' Based', ' on', ' the', ' ticket', ',', ' this', ' appears', ' to', ' be', ' a', ' bug', '_report', ' …'];
const dist = [
  { label: 'bug_report', p: 0.97 },
  { label: 'feature_request', p: 0.03 },
];
---

<figure class="diagram">
  <p class="weights">Same frozen weights, same ticket</p>
  <div class="cols">
    <div class="col">
      <p class="label">Readout for a person</p>
      <ol class="tokens" aria-label="Tokens generated one at a time">
        {prose.map((t) => <li>{t.replace(/^ /, ' ')}</li>)}
      </ol>
      <p class="cost">
        <strong>One forward pass per token</strong>, strictly in order. Token 13 can't start until token 12
        exists.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="col typed">
      <p class="label">Readout for software</p>
      <ul class="bars">
        {
          dist.map((d) => (
            <li>
              <code>{d.label}</code>
              <span class="track">
                <span class="fill" style={`width:${Math.round(d.p * 100)}%`} />
              </span>
              <span class="p">{d.p.toFixed(2)}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p class="cost">
        <strong>One pass</strong>, answers constrained to the options you defined. More questions run in
        parallel.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    The decision is the same on both sides. The left side spends most of its work translating it into
    English for a reader that, in production, is usually a parser. (Probabilities from the example
    response in TypeSafe's docs.)
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .weights {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;
    border: 1px dashed var(--text-3);
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }
  .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .label {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-3);
  }
  .tokens {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .tokens li {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.35rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--role-change);
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--role-change) 10%, var(--surface));
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    white-space: pre;
  }
  .bars {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .bars li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 8.5rem 1fr 2.5rem;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
  .bars code {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }
  .track {
    height: 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: var(--surface-2);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .fill {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    background: var(--role-done);
  }
  .p {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    text-align: right;
  }
  .cost {
    margin: auto 0 0 !important;
    padding-top: 0.9rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .bars li {
      grid-template-columns: 7.5rem 1fr 2.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
